{"seq":4,"id":"Q1","type":"question","at":"2026-10-21T15:19:16Z","by":"AC2","prev":"sha256:bed666eb9a20bc4ca5f35b48541dc953334d68aa1f6d7d5c9231b27a5328c710","content_hash":"sha256:a55314d41e6f699806b2e81e64277c98c6f8cfe2087d97a6022be406f3d93409","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"text":"Which criterion decides whether a pure additive lagged SSOE model (ADAM notation, components with different lags, including GUM) forgets its initial states, and how can it be computed efficiently inside the estimation loop?"}}
{"seq":5,"id":"NT1","type":"note","at":"2026-10-21T15:19:16Z","by":"AC2","prev":"sha256:22d11d8ec202e815fe9fc856a0a05b33f606c93f73e11a6a11743657a874f33a","content_hash":"sha256:c4df40f92e62fe4b6327cc67698b591afe495ebc6f6d8ea78519bbd4fd1939be","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"text":"Before this record was started, the agent ran unrecorded numpy checks (in a scratchpad, not in the repository) while designing the checker for issue openforecast-org/smooth#415 with the human. Those checks shaped the criterion and the hypotheses below. Their code was consolidated into .claude/research/eigenChecker and is re-run here as exploratory run(s), so that every number used later comes from a recorded run."}}
{"seq":6,"id":"DC1","type":"decision","at":"2026-10-21T15:19:16Z","by":"AC2","prev":"sha256:d325db51f31ef63005f9c281b2e265d652da54cfd5a6211a74cbf97354fb0689","content_hash":"sha256:da69ccb53be808a117170c708a13b3f391982b5ae5c92368a82d9b68c5c82b90","supersedes":null,"origin":null,"body":{"text":"Prototype in numpy before the R/C++ implementation: the criterion is the invertibility of the MA polynomial theta(B) = det(I - D L(B)) of the model's ARIMA form, after cancelling the cyclotomic factors it shares with phi(B) = det(I - F L(B)), with coefficients from an inverse DFT and the decision from the step-down (Schur-Cohn) recursion."}}
